<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gangaraja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gangaraja was the leading general and minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnuvardhana">Vishnuvardhana</a>, who captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talakad">Talakad</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> in 1116. A devout Jain, he restored and endowed many Jain shrines, especially at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shravanabelagola">Shravanabelagola</a>, where numerous inscriptions record his donations and his military deeds.</p></div>
